# The launcher's update check finding a newer Non-Visual Melee release in a
# canned release list: the update banner at start with the release's version,
# title and description, its buttons, and Settings' Updates row, before and
# after Check now. Run in launcher mode, with accessibility on but muted and
# the canned list read in place of GitHub's (as run_level.py runs it):
#   python tools/a11y/drive.py --launcher --muted --update-list tools/a11y/update_lists/newer.json tools/a11y/launcher_update.drive
# newer.json holds ci-latest, a draft, a release without the Windows zip,
# a11y-v99.0.0 with it, a11y-v0.0.0 and two base port releases, so the
# offer is 99.0.0 whatever src/pc/a11y/FORK_VERSION holds. drive.py refuses
# to press the banner's Open release page and View Release, which open the
# browser.

# The banner comes up beside the opening, its version first.
wait '"Melee launcher\. Ready to play'
wait '"Update available: 99\.0\.0"$'
wait '"Non-Visual Melee 99\.0\.0 beta"$'
wait '"A newer version of Non-Visual Melee is available \(99\.0\.0\)\. Download and extract the Windows ZIP from the release page\."$'

# Its buttons come before Play.
key Up
wait '"Later, button\. Hide this until the next start\."$'
key Up
wait '"View Release, button\. '
key Up
wait '"Open release page, button\. '
key Down Down Down
wait '"Play, button\. '

# Settings' Updates row says the offer, and Check now reads the list again.
key Down Down Down
wait '"Settings, button\. '
key Return
wait '"Settings\. Graphics\. '
key Up Up
wait '"Launcher\. '
key Right
wait '"Interface size, '
key Down Down
wait '"Updates: Check now, button\. Update available: Non-Visual Melee 99\.0\.0\. Look for a new release now\."$'
key Return
wait '"Checking for updates\.\.\."$'
wait '"Update available: Non-Visual Melee 99\.0\.0"$'
